     "page": 1,
     "text": "Bryant Inc Clinic\n\nRe: Rachel Terrell (DOB Life Insurer,\n\nI hope this letter finds you well. I am writing to provide you with a summary of Ms. Rachel Terrell's medical history, focusing primarily on her Anemia / blood disorders and related visits. \n\nOn November 19, 2024, Ms. Terrell visited our clinic regarding her ongoing Anemia / blood disorders. During her visit, her blood pressure was recorded at 124/64, and her weight was 99 pounds. Ms. Terrell has been managing her Anemia / blood disorders, which include venous thromboembolism and sickle cell disease, for several years now. Her condition remains controlled, and she has been compliant with the treatment plan.\n\nMs. Terrell was also seen on May 27, 2024, for the same reason. At that time, her blood pressure was 119/66, and she weighed 105 pounds. She reported feeling well and was doing well overall.\n\nOn December 3, 2023, Ms. Terrell visited for a medication refill. Her blood pressure was 121/64, and her weight was 103 pounds. Her Anemia / blood disorders (with vte and sickle cell disease) were reviewed, and her condition remained stable and controlled.\n\nThe visit on June 9, 2023, was also for Anemia / blood Her blood pressure was 133/72, and she weighed 102 pounds. Ms. Terrell was doing well, and there were no new issues reported.\n\nOn December 15, 2022, Ms. Terrell came in for follow-up regarding her Anemia / blood disorders. Her blood pressure was 130/72, and her weight was 97 pounds. She continues to manage her condition effectively, with her Anemia / blood disorders (vte and sickle cell disease) remaining well-controlled.\n\nJune 21, 2022, saw another visit for Anemia / blood disorders. At that time, her blood pressure was 131/63, and she weighed 106 pounds. Ms. Terrell was doing well, with no new concerns reported.\n\nOn December 27, 2021, Ms. Terrell visited for a follow-up on her Anemia / blood disorders. Her blood pressure was 121/71, and she weighed 98 pounds. She was doing well, and her condition was stable.\n\nSocial history reveals that Ms. Terrell used to smoke cigarettes, consuming about 10 per day. She started this habit on November 29, 2016, and quit on July 22, 2024. She also consumes approximately six alcoholic drinks per week.\n\nPlease let me know you require any additional information.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Adam Bright\nHematology, Bryant Inc Clinic\n\n---\n\nThis document contains all relevant medical information pertaining to Ms. Rachel Terrell, as requested. you need any further details, please do not hesitate to contact me.\n\nBest regards,\n\nDr. Adam Bright\n"
